course: dictionary
lesson: 5395
title: A word from the vegetable patch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may not know every word in a text, but the words around it often give you clues. This is called context. Read the sentence again and ask: what kind of word would fit here?
explain: «Broccoli, cabbage, cauliflower, kale, Brussels sprouts and kohlrabi are all one species.» The words before kohlrabi are all vegetables, so kohlrabi is probably a vegetable too. Swap in your meaning: "kohlrabi is a vegetable" still makes sense, so your guess is a good one.
explain: The dictionary tells you more. Kohlrabi has a round, swollen stem that grows just above the ground, and you can eat it raw or cooked. Context gave you the first clue, and the meaning confirmed it.
fact: Kohlrabi is a vegetable of the cabbage family.
fact: The round, swollen part of a kohlrabi is its stem, and it grows just above the ground.
fact: You can eat kohlrabi raw or cooked.
fact: Kohlrabi is green or purple, and it tastes like mild cabbage or broccoli stem.
fact: «Bred» means grown by people who choose plants and keep the best ones for growing again.
exercise: What is kohlrabi? | *A vegetable of the cabbage family | A bird that lives on the cliffs | A tool for digging | A kind of wild flower
exercise: «Broccoli, cabbage, cauliflower, kale, Brussels sprouts and kohlrabi are all one species.» What kind of thing is kohlrabi most likely to be? | A musical instrument | *A vegetable | A planet
exercise: Where does the round, swollen stem of a kohlrabi grow? | Deep under the soil, like a carrot | Under the sea | Up in the air on a tall tree | *Just above the ground
test: How can you eat kohlrabi? | Only as a drink | *Raw or cooked | Only raw, never cooked | Only when it is purple
test: In «all one species, bred by farmers», what does bred mean? | Thrown away | *Grown by people who choose the best plants | Eaten in winter | Lost in the field
exam: What does kohlrabi taste like? | Sweet, like sugar | Salty, like the sea | Sour, like a lemon | *Mild, like cabbage or broccoli stem
